  "limitations": [
    "Host hook spans measure dispatch, driver work and any internal blocking; they do not attribute exclusive GPU execution to layers.",
    "The unhooked remainder includes model Python work, layout/state handling, record metadata/append bookkeeping and wrapper overhead; it is not a pure Python cost estimate.",
    "Original finite_check_and_wait includes previously enqueued current-packet model work plus concatenation, isfinite, reduction and scalar readback. It is not the cost of validation alone.",
    "Split-wait adds a completion barrier and reports post-completion finite-check cost. This changes scheduling and batching, so it cannot supply an exact subtraction from the unsplit public API.",
    "Public API synchronizes and returns CPU-ready output for every packet. No unfinished previous-packet work can accumulate from these serial calls. A paced slowdown is not evidence of previous-packet GPU queue backlog.",
    "Paced schedule sleeps toward 80ms absolute targets, but actual scheduled-arrival/start/completion timestamps and lateness are not recorded. All observed public service times are below80ms, but these short bursts do not establish sustained real-time deadlines.",
    "Only two order-reversed repetitions of8packets are present; public unpaced steady means drift from5.3357 to8.1632ms. No causal power/clock/scheduler/queue explanation follows.",
    "Output byte hashes agree across phases/routes for each matching packet. This audit does not independently rerun original-ONNX numerical or history checks.",
    "Input hashes bind supplied snapshots only; profiler snapshots themselves do not pin model source, weights, generated-module contents or device identity. Existing qualification/provenance must be cited separately.",
    "No GPU, model, build or benchmark execution was performed by this audit."
  ]
}
